# ENT-15 — Enterprise Documentation & Runbook

Durable lock: `docs/architecture/enterprise-documentation-runbook-governance.md`.

- The mandatory runbook set lives under `docs/runbooks/` and is declared in
  `config/enterprise_documentation.php`. It is **enforced**, not docs-only, by
  `scripts`/`config` + `foundation:enterprise-documentation-check --strict`.
- Every runbook must be actionable: purpose, when to use, prerequisites, safe
  commands, forbidden commands, evidence, rollback/fallback, troubleshooting,
  smoke verification, security/PII notes, owner/reviewer, review cadence.
- Destructive commands (`migrate:fresh`, `db:wipe`, `schema:drop`,
  `migrate:reset`) may appear **only** inside a runbook forbidden/warning section
  and are documented as forbidden. Those literals live in config, not scanner code.
- Docs never contain secrets, credentials, the environment file, or unmasked
  KTP/NIK; every doc passes the release-evidence forbidden-pattern/regex scan.
- The runbook set collectively references every ENT-5..15 foundation readiness
  command; `docs:enterprise-runbook-summary` renders the registry read-only.
- Evidence `enterprise-documentation-check.json` is required in ci/vps profiles and
  as a release-safety pre-deploy gate; not committed to git.
- Any new runbook / section / topic / command reference must extend
  `config/enterprise_documentation.php` + tests and stay green under:
  `php artisan foundation:enterprise-documentation-check --strict`.
- Preserve ENT-5..14: this gate re-verifies queue-retry, idempotency/outbox,
  developer-console, health-check, security-compliance, CI/CD gate, deploy/rollback,
  backup/DR, load-test-baseline, and scale-projection governance.
